-- doers for what this session found and could not change in the same piece of work
INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT 'BP26-PROVENANCE-BASIS-1: the provenance sidecar says its content hash covers the .md text, which has YAML front matter ahead of the hashed body',
'Charter pillar: research. Serves BP26-PROVENANCE-MARKING-1 (agent_issues 1000335, roadmap row 1391) and the verify-without-the-worker recipe of docs/BP26-SECURITY-CLUSTER.md.

Evidence read 2026-11-05 after the signing key went live: https://papers.qnfo.org/papers/twisted-cuprate-twistronics/provenance.json verifies from /.well-known/provenance-key.json with node:crypto (kid match, Ed25519 true), but its subject.content_sha256 (06f661c6...) is not the sha256 of the text served at subject.url + ".md": that text starts with YAML front matter (--- title: ... ---). The hash equals the sha256 of the same text after the closing --- line and the one blank line after it, which is body_md. content_basis says "body_md (UTF-8), the text served at <url>.md", so a reader who follows it literally gets a mismatch and concludes the paper was altered.

Change in qnfo-gateway: provStatement builds subject.content_basis as "body_md (UTF-8): the text served at <url>.md after its YAML front matter and the blank line that follows it" (the hash stays as it is, so every signed sidecar and every asset_provenance row stays valid). Add a case to qnfo-gateway/provenance.test.mjs that fetches the .md text of a fixture paper, strips the front matter as described and checks the hash.

Closing probe: runtime-probe below.

code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-gateway/worker.js
code-anchor: async function provStatement(paper, p, kid) {
runtime-probe: {"url": "https://papers.qnfo.org/papers/twisted-cuprate-twistronics/provenance.json", "status": 200, "contains": "after its YAML front matter"}',
'bp26-provenance', 'reliability', 'medium', 'open', datetime('now'), datetime('now')
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE status = 'open' AND title LIKE 'BP26-PROVENANCE-BASIS-1:%');

INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT 'BP26-KILLSWITCH-READERS-2: qnfo-cloud-ops reads fleet_kill_switch once per scheduled run and stops new side effects while it is on',
'Charter pillar: autonomy. Serves BP26-KILLSWITCH-READERS-1 (roadmap row 1722, catalogue 3.4). Readers live: qnfo-deploy-guard 1.4.0, qnfo-code-orchestrator 0.48.0, qnfo-github-steward 0.17.0. Pending in docs/KILL-SWITCH-DRILL.md: qnfo-fleet-control, qnfo-ops, qnfo-social, qnfo-research-exec, qnfo-cloud-ops. qnfo-cloud-ops is the next reader because no session holds its file (work-locks read 2026-11-05) and every cron it runs goes through one function.

Change in qnfo-cloud-ops: runScheduledJob reads ops_config.fleet_kill_switch once per run (cached 30 seconds, like killSwitchOn and killSwitchObserved in qnfo-github-steward/worker.js), fails open (an unreadable row is off, recorded as failed_open), and while the flag is on skips the job body and records one kill-switch.observed event (job qnfo-cloud-ops); jobs that only keep bookkeeping alive (the heartbeat, logRun) keep running so the drill can see resumption. Add the version-bump note, qnfo-cloud-ops/kill-switch.test.mjs (flag on skips a job, off runs it, unreadable runs it and records failed_open, the cache holds for 30 seconds), the row in the readers table of docs/KILL-SWITCH-DRILL.md and the line qnfo-cloud-ops in KS_READERS of scripts/cf_ops_actions.py in the pull request that makes the deployed version live.

Closing probe: the next kill-switch drill lists qnfo-cloud-ops under readers; until then the code-probe below.

